<section id="which-mode" class="city-section" aria-labelledby="which-mode-title">
  <h2 id="which-mode-title">Which mode when</h2>
  <p class="which-mode-lede">Each task gets the ceremony it needs. Nothing more.</p>
  <div class="which-mode-table-wrap">
    <table class="which-mode-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Mode</th>
          <th scope="col">Task</th>
          <th scope="col">Ceremony</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row"><code class="which-mode-tag">direct</code></th>
          <td>Questions and small edits.</td>
          <td>The main agent answers or edits directly. No plan. No approval.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row"><code class="which-mode-tag">plan</code></th>
          <td>Large or risky work: more than about 3 files, or auth, data, CI, or infra.</td>
          <td>A plan first. In Claude Code that is plan mode, so the plan is written on Opus. You approve it.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row"><code class="which-mode-tag">hybrid</code></th>
          <td>Lots of independent new code.</td>
          <td><code>claude --agent lead-dev-hybrid</code>. Opus plans and reviews. File-disjoint parts go to headless opencode and agy workers in their own git worktrees. Each branch is re-tested before it is merged.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <th scope="row"><code class="which-mode-tag">subagents</code></th>
          <td>Work that does not split, or touches auth, secrets, or data, or no worker is installed.</td>
          <td>lead-dev-hybrid keeps it on Claude subagents. Never on a cold worker.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="which-mode-rule">Hybrid pays off with writing volume, not file count: small tasks cost more than doing them directly.</p>
</section>

<style>
